  "adaptation": {
    "semantic": "Some languages use one word for the hair on the head and another for hair on the body or for an animal's fur; English **hair** can cover all three.",
    "grammar": "**Hair** on the head (sense 1) is uncountable and takes a singular verb: *her hair is long*. The plural **hairs** means single threads (*two gray hairs*).",
